course: dictionary
lesson: 14545
title: Peruse: read it carefully, or just look
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peruse is a formal word. It means to read or look at something carefully and in detail. «Please peruse the passage before you answer the questions.» The writer wants you to read every line slowly, not skim it.
explain: Many people now use peruse more casually, to mean look through something quickly or browse. «Sam perused the shelves of the toy shop.» He was probably not studying every toy; he was just looking along the shelves. The context tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like «passage», «document» or «carefully» point to careful reading. Words like «shelves» or «at your leisure» point to looking casually. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Peruse is a verb: peruse, peruses, perused, perusing.
fact: «Peruse» means to read or look at something carefully and in detail.
fact: Informally, «peruse» can mean to look through something casually or browse.
fact: «Peruse the menu» means read the menu to choose your food.
fact: In maths, «peruse the problem» means read the problem carefully before you start. It does not change the numbers.
exercise: «Please peruse the passage before you answer.» What does peruse mean here? | To tear it up | To hum a tune about it | *To read it carefully and in detail | To count the letters in it
exercise: «Sam perused the shelves of the toy shop, not really looking for anything.» What does peruse mean here? | *To look through casually, or browse | To buy every toy on the shelf | To read a whole book aloud | To clean the shelves
exercise: Which word in «She perused the contract before she signed it» is a clue that she read carefully? | *contract | dog | sunny | walked
test: «Peruse the menu.» In a restaurant, what should you do? | Eat the menu | *Read the menu to choose your food | Throw the menu away | Sing to the waiter
test: Which word means the same as browse, in its casual sense? | To jump | *To peruse | To shout | To sleep
exam: In «Peruse the instructions carefully before you start», what does peruse mean? | Eat the instructions | Glue them to the wall | Sing them quietly | *Read them carefully and in detail
